CurrentAPI based on <a href="http://www.jsonrpc.org/specification" target="_blank">JSON-RPC 2.0</a> with <a href="http://oauth.net/2/" target="_blank">OAuth 2.0</a> as authorization.<br />OAuth enpoints are <a href="https://myshows.me/oauth/authorize" target="_blank">https://myshows.me/oauth/authorize</a> and <a href="https://myshows.me/oauth/token" target="_blank">https://myshows.me/oauth/token</a>.<br />We use <b>Bearer</b> access token implementation and we only one scope <b>basic</b>.<br /><br />To request OAuth AppId please contact us <a href="mailto:api@myshows.me">api@myshows.me</a>.<br /><h4>Example</h4><br /><div class="content"><div class="block curl"><pre style="word-wrap: break-word; white-space: pre-wrap;">curl -X POST --header "Content-Type: application/json" --header "Accept: application/json" --header "Authorization: Bearer 859ea2450228a5d655e3a8c2f9a5aedc30b591df" --header "Accept-Language: en" -d "{
  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",
  \"method\": \"shows.GetById\",
  \"params\": {
    \"showId\": 1,
    \"withEpisodes\": true
  },
  \"id\": 1
}" "https://api.myshows.me/v2/rpc/"</pre></div></div><br />We also support <a href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6749#section-4.3" target="_blank">Resource Owner Password Credentials Grant</a> for devices without browser.<br /><br /><h4>Example</h4><br /><div class="content"><div class="block curl"><pre style="word-wrap: break-word; white-space: pre-wrap;">curl "https://myshows.me/oauth/token" -d "grant_type=password&client_id=&client_secret=&username=&password="</pre></div></div>
